From fc93b9b72488a76ed5dcdfe5d0946ae644e9dd92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:23:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Let the container write to its own data directory
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`docker-compose.yml` mounts a named volume at `/app/data`, and the app writes
classrooms, classroom jobs, uploaded materials and usage records there —
`lib/server/classroom-storage.ts`, `lib/server/materials/bytes.ts` and
`lib/server/usage-storage.ts` all resolve under it. The Dockerfile never creates
that path, so Docker creates the mount point when it seeds the volume, and a
fresh named volume covering a path absent from the image comes up root-owned:

    $ docker exec ... ls -ld /app/data
    drwxr-xr-x 2 root root /app/data
    $ docker exec ... id
    uid=1001(nextjs) gid=65533(nogroup)

Every write then fails. Observed once every few seconds in a running container:

    [WARN] [UsageStorage] Failed to record usage (ignored):
      Error: EACCES: permission denied, mkdir '/app/data/usage'

Usage records are swallowed with a warning, which is why this survives unnoticed;
the classroom and material paths are on the same directory and are not obviously
so forgiving.

Creating the directory as the runtime user before `USER nextjs` fixes it at the
source: Docker seeds a new named volume with the ownership of the image path it
covers, so the volume comes up writable. Existing volumes were created under the
old behaviour and keep their root ownership — those need a one-off
`chown 1001:1001 /app/data` from a privileged container.
---
 integration/maic/Dockerfile | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/integration/maic/Dockerfile b/integration/maic/Dockerfile
index d4faad060..37a19532b 100644
--- a/integration/maic/Dockerfile
+++ b/integration/maic/Dockerfile
@@ -107,6 +107,14 @@ COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public
 COPY --from=builder --chown=nextjs:nodejs /app/.next/standalone ./
 COPY --from=builder --chown=nextjs:nodejs /app/.next/static ./.next/static
 
+# Create the data directory as the runtime user before dropping privileges.
+# docker-compose.yml mounts a named volume here, and Docker seeds a fresh named
+# volume with the ownership of the image path it covers — so when that path does
+# not exist in the image, the mount point is created root-owned and `nextjs`
+# cannot write to its own data directory. Classrooms, materials and usage all
+# land here, and every write fails with EACCES.
+RUN mkdir -p /app/data && chown -R nextjs:nodejs /app/data
+
 USER nextjs
 
 EXPOSE 3000
-- 
